   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 371 of the laws of 1998, amending the public\nauthorities law relating to the construction and financing of facilities by\nthe dormitory authority for the New York State Rehabilitation Association, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5711",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5711-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 371 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5711\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 371 of the laws of 1998, amending the public\nauthorities law relating to the construction and financing of facilities\nby the dormitory authority for the New York State Rehabilitation Associ-\nation, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend, until December 31, 2028, the\nauthorization for New York State Rehabilitation Association, and its\nsuccessor organization, now known as the New York Alliance for Inclusion\nand Innovation, to receive construction management and financial\nservices from the Dormitory of the State of New York (DASNY).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would extend, until December 31, 2028, the\nauthorization for New York State Rehabilitation Association, and its\nsuccessor organization, now known as the New York Alliance for Inclusion\nand Innovation, to receive construction management and financial\nservices from the Dormitory of the State of New York.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York Alliance for Inclusion and Innovation, formerly known as\nthe New York State Rehabilitation Association, is a private, non-profit\nstatewide organization providing leadership and advocacy on multiple\nmatters of public policy on behalf of disabilities providers and the\nindividuals they serve. Additionally, the Alliance informs, educates,\nand supports association members in their effort to offer a diverse\nspectrum of services and helps integrate people with differing abilities\ninto the community. In 2018, the New York State Rehabilitation Associ-\nation received approval to merge with another statewide disability asso-\nciation to become the New York Alliance for Inclusion and Innovation.\n\nExpiration of the bonding authority would harm significant bond initi-\natives, resulting in lost savings to the State and lost funding to rein-\nvest in critical support and services to individuals with disabilities.\nThis bill would benefit the taxpayers of the State and individuals\nserved by New York Alliance for Inclusion and Innovation's member agen-\ncies by extending the authority to utilize construction and management\nservices through DASNY until December 31, 2028.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE ISTORY:\n\n2018: S.8815 (Ortt)- Chapter 169 of the Laws of 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
